1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,292
This is CaliDoc, by Mohammed Hamdan and Mohamed
Cheriet, from the Synchromedia

2
00:00:06,292 --> 00:00:08,418
Laboratory at ÉTS Montréal.

3
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:15,034
It asks a simple question: when a document
extractor comes with a conformal

4
00:00:15,034 --> 00:00:18,844
guarantee, what exactly is that
guarantee about?

5
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:27,622
On SROIE, a strong LayoutLMv3-Large tagger with
token-level conformal prediction at

6
00:00:27,622 --> 00:00:31,571
a 90% target covers 89.8% of tokens.

7
00:00:32,024 --> 00:00:34,903
By the usual criterion,
calibration worked.

8
00:00:35,356 --> 00:00:39,988
Yet of 420 gold field spans, not one
has every token covered.

9
00:00:40,766 --> 00:00:47,891
The single marginal threshold is sized for the O
class, 84% of tokens, so all four

10
00:00:47,891 --> 00:00:54,930
field-initial B classes get zero coverage, and
every field starts with a B token.

11
00:00:56,330 --> 00:01:02,226
On a real test receipt, every field's worst word
lies beyond the token-marginal

12
00:01:02,226 --> 00:01:07,301
threshold, yet inside the field thresholds
that CaliDoc calibrates.

13
00:01:07,661 --> 00:01:13,895
So we change the calibrated object to the complete
field, with the document as the

14
00:01:13,895 --> 00:01:17,925
exchangeable unit, and leave the
extractor untouched.

15
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:25,388
Each span is scored by its worst word, which turns
full-span coverage into a scalar

16
00:01:25,388 --> 00:01:25,973
problem.

17
00:01:26,553 --> 00:01:32,392
Conformal risk control over documents then bounds
the expected fraction of missed

18
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:34,483
fields per document by alpha.

19
00:01:34,971 --> 00:01:41,377
That is an expectation: not a promise about any
single document or field type, and

20
00:01:41,377 --> 00:01:45,048
the coverage numbers that follow
are empirical.

21
00:01:46,450 --> 00:01:52,421
Field types with enough calibration spans get
their own thresholds; low-support

22
00:01:52,421 --> 00:01:58,014
types fall back to the pooled threshold and
inherit only the pooled bound.

23
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:08,836
On SROIE, realized field-miss risk falls from
1.000 to 0.091, full-span coverage

24
00:02:08,836 --> 00:02:17,463
rises from zero to 0.909, and span CovGap falls
from 90 points to 2.1, for sets

25
00:02:17,463 --> 00:02:19,460
about ten percent larger.

26
00:02:20,122 --> 00:02:25,312
Where the marginal threshold already worked,
results stay roughly unchanged.

27
00:02:25,892 --> 00:02:32,993
CORD, with sparse field support, pays a 3.2-fold
set-size cost; a level-calibrated

28
00:02:32,993 --> 00:02:36,701
variant reduces it under the
pooled bound only.

29
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:44,432
The same threshold drives an annotation audit: do
escaped words concentrate at field

30
00:02:44,432 --> 00:02:47,899
boundaries, the signature of
alignment errors?

31
00:02:48,479 --> 00:02:54,458
A conditional randomization null with Holm
correction answers it, assuming

32
00:02:54,458 --> 00:03:00,756
independence across spans, and every finding
must agree with a document-blocked

33
00:03:00,756 --> 00:03:01,553
bootstrap.

34
00:03:02,950 --> 00:03:08,267
The audit flags SROIE ADDRESS and COMPANY, and
nothing on the clean benchmarks.

35
00:03:08,848 --> 00:03:16,003
After an independent re-alignment of the labels,
ADDRESS enrichment falls from 4.07

36
00:03:16,003 --> 00:03:19,691
to 0.79, and nothing is rejected.

37
00:03:20,109 --> 00:03:24,591
The repair came from re-alignment,
not from calibration.

38
00:03:25,990 --> 00:03:33,036
Closest prior work certifies a representative
token per entity; CaliDoc certifies

39
00:03:33,036 --> 00:03:36,903
the complete field, as a
document-level risk.

40
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:45,486
The limits: the guarantee is a risk, not a
coverage; field-conditional calibration

41
00:03:45,486 --> 00:03:52,322
is support-limited; fields of two words or fewer
are untestable; and real-data

42
00:03:52,322 --> 00:03:54,600
validation rests on SROIE.

43
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,332
Report reliability for the object
you actually deliver.

44
00:03:59,913 --> 00:04:05,009
Code, checkpoints, the supplement and a
Colab demo are linked.

45
00:04:05,323 --> 00:04:06,124
Thank you.

